  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2406.12040v2</id>
    <title>Critical wetting in the (2+1)D Solid-On-Solid model</title>
    <updated>2024-09-23T13:48:10Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.12040v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2406.12040v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>In this note, we study the low temperature $(2+1)$D SOS interface above a hard floor with critical pinning potential $λ_w= \log (\frac{1}{1-e^{-4β}})$. At $λ&lt;λ_w$ entropic repulsion causes the surface to delocalize and be rigid at height $\frac1{4β}\log n+O(1)$; at $λ&gt;λ_w$ it is localized at some $O(1)$ height. We show that at $λ=λ_w$, there is delocalization, with rigidity now at height $\lfloor \frac1{6β}\log n+\frac13\rfloor$, confirming a conjecture of Lacoin.</summary>
    <category term="math.PR" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="math-ph" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2024-06-17T19:19:50Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>12 pages</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="math.PR"/>
